ggml-cpu vec: vectorize ggml_vec_max_f32 on arm64

The scalar loop compiles to 64 dependent fcmp/fcsel pairs (clang does not vectorize float max without fast-math).
The tiled flash-attention kernel calls it for every row of every 64x64 Q/KV tile, so on arm64 it was about 10-15% of
the kernel (derived from instruction latency, scratchpad bughunt asm). Max is order-independent, so the result is the
same value; only the sign of a zero maximum can differ, which cancels in the softmax subtraction that uses it.
Correctness: arm64 under QEMU (0001-0008 plus a first 0009 that never ran, MiniCPM5 and Ling, 256 tokens): KL divergence against stock at the
tool's floor (max 3.7e-5, same top token 100%). Phone speed: not measured yet.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.h b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.h
index f24fa00f2..7231158ec 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.h
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.h
@@ -1678,7 +1678,22 @@ inline static void ggml_vec_sum_bf16_ggf(const int n, float * s, const ggml_bf16
 }
 
